//? Title: NEAT topology evolution on XOR
//? Lang: en

> NEAT topology evolution on XOR

NeuroEvolution of Augmenting Topologies (NEAT) searches over connection
weights and network structure. The 64 networks start with inputs and a
bias feeding one tanh output. A mutation can perturb weights, add a
forward connection, or split an existing connection to introduce a
hidden node. The population records the same innovation ID whenever
independent mutations add the same connection. Crossover uses these IDs
to align genes across networks of different shapes.

Each generation groups networks by compatibility distance. Networks
join the first species whose representative is close enough. Species
are sampled in proportion to their mean fitness, then tournaments
select parents within the chosen species. This gives small species a
chance to reproduce while new structures are still developing.

The plot shows the best fitness across all four XOR cases. Fitness
equals the reciprocal of one plus mean squared prediction error on
targets of −1 and +1. The table also reports sign accuracy, which can
fall even when squared error improves. This seeded three-update run
demonstrates topology growth and lineage, and ends before solving XOR.

[Stanley and Miikkulainen (2002), Evolving Neural Networks through Augmenting Topologies|https://doi.org/10.1162/106365602320169811]

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/neat.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

int main() {
  namespace n=dm::nn;
  constexpr int count=64;
  std::mt19937 rng(47501);
  n::Neat population(2,count,rng);
  const auto features=n::from_vector<float>({-1,-1,-1,1,1,-1,1,1},{4,2});
  const std::array targets{-1.f,1.f,1.f,-1.f};
  auto parents=n::from_vector(std::vector<int>(2*count,-1),{count,2});
  std::vector<double> history;
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  std::print("| Generation | Species | Genomes with hidden nodes | Best fitness | Correct signs |\n"
             "|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n");
  for (int generation=0;generation<=3;++generation) {
    const auto output=population.predict(features);
    const auto predictions=output.to_vector<float>();
    std::vector<float> fitness(count);
    for (int i=0;i<count;++i) {
      float error=0;
      for (int sample=0;sample<4;++sample) {
        error+=std::pow(predictions[4*i+sample]-targets[sample],2)/4;
      }
      fitness[i]=1.f/(1.f+error);
    }
    const auto best=std::max_element(fitness.begin(),fitness.end())-fitness.begin();
    history.push_back(fitness[best]);
    const auto groups=population.species();
    std::vector<int> species(count);
    for (std::size_t group=0;group<groups.size();++group) {
      for (int member:groups[group]) species[member]=static_cast<int>(group);
    }
    const auto innovations=population.innovations();
    std::vector<float> genes(count*innovations*4,-1.f);
    int hidden=0;
    for (int row=0;row<count;++row) {
      bool has_hidden=false;
      for (const auto& [id,gene]:population.genomes()[row]) {
        auto* entry=genes.data()+4*(row*innovations+id);
        entry[0]=gene.from;
        entry[1]=gene.to;
        entry[2]=gene.weight;
        entry[3]=gene.enabled;
        has_hidden|=gene.to>3 && gene.enabled;
      }
      hidden+=has_hidden;
    }
    std::vector<int> splits;
    for (const auto& [edge,node]:population.splits()) splits.insert(splits.end(),{edge,node});
    int correct=0;
    for (int i=0;i<4;++i) correct+=(predictions[4*best+i]>0)==(targets[i]>0);
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {:.6f} | {} / 4 |\n",generation,groups.size(),hidden,history.back(),correct);
    n::save_npz(std::format("build/neat_generation{}.npz",generation),{
        {"genes",n::from_vector(genes,{count,static_cast<std::int64_t>(innovations),4})},
        {"depth",n::from_vector(population.depths())},{"output",output},
        {"fitness",n::from_vector(fitness)},{"species",n::from_vector(species)},
        {"parents",parents},{"splits",n::from_vector(splits,{static_cast<std::int64_t>(splits.size()/2),2})}});
    if (generation<3) parents=population.evolve(fitness,rng);
  }
  auto plot=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  plot.lines({0,1,2,3},history,"Best fitness",{37,99,235})
      .points({0,1,2,3},history,dm::RGBA{37,99,235})
      .title("NEAT on XOR").x_label("Generation").y_label("Best fitness")
      .size(800,460).save_svg("build/neat.svg");
}
```
